## Visual Studio und Projektausschluss
# Exclude the Visual Studio user-specific settings directory
.vs/

# Exclude all 'bin' and 'obj' directories
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/

# Exclude NuGet packages directory
# This might not be necessary if you are restoring packages, but is safe to include.
packages/

# Exclude user-specific files
*.user
*.suo

# Exclude temporary files and build artifacts
*.pdb
*.Designer.cs
*.cache
*.log

# Exclude the project's output folder for different configurations
*/[Dd]ebug/
*/[Rr]elease/

# Exclusion for Rider/ReSharper
.idea/

# Exclude compiled output and deployment artifacts
*.exe
*.dll
*.appx
*.pri

# Exclude the VSIX ID file that caused the error in your screenshot
# .vs/Projektarbeit_M346/FileContentIndex/83545f59-d8b6-4099-964c-cf42960a46f2.vsidx
# The general rule .vs/ covers this, but adding the specific file type too:
*.vsidx